---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

// Devkeep has its own brand (navy/gold, Fraunces/IBM Plex, light + dark), so
// this page deliberately doesn't import site.css or the site Header/Footer --
// see docs/PRODUCT.md item 6. Its styles below are global but only ship on
// this page.
---

<Layout
  title="Devkeep Alpha Program — StarterCulture"
  description="Devkeep: one shell, one login, six purpose-built developer tools — all reading the same living product doc. Now looking for alpha testers."
>
  <Fragment slot="head">
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Fraunces:ital,opsz,wght@0,9..144,500;0,9..144,600;1,9..144,500;1,9..144,600&family=IBM+Plex+Sans:wght@400;500;600&family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" />
  </Fragment>

<!-- ============================================================ HERO -->
<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-inner wrap">
    <div class="badge lg" aria-hidden="true">
      <svg viewBox="0 0 140 140" role="img"><title>Devkeep</title>
        <rect width="140" height="140" rx="28" fill="#23264D"/>
        <path d="M48,30.9 L24,70 L48,109.1" fill="none" stroke="#FFFFFF" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <path d="M92,30.9 L116,70 L92,109.1" fill="none" stroke="#FFFFFF" stroke-width="6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        <rect x="60.34" y="50.80" width="19.32" height="55.20" fill="#D9A441"/>
        <rect x="60.34" y="38.80" width="4.14" height="12.00" fill="#D9A441"/>
        <rect x="67.93" y="34.00" width="4.14" height="16.80" fill="#D9A441"/>
        <rect x="75.52" y="38.80" width="4.14" height="12.00" fill="#D9A441"/>
        <rect x="67.93" y="62.80" width="4.14" height="7.20" fill="#23264D"/>
      </svg>
    </div>
    <div class="eyebrow" style="justify-content:center;">alpha program — open now</div>
    <div class="hero-textblock">
      <div class="hero-brackets" aria-hidden="true">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 40 140"><path d="M32,10 L8,70 L32,130" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        <svg viewBox="0 0 40 140"><path d="M8,10 L32,70 L8,130" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
      </div>
      <div class="hero-textblock-inner">
        <h1>Devkeep</h1>
        <p class="tagline">Your code is your kingdom. Every kingdom needs a keep.</p>
        <p class="lede hero-lede">One shell, one login, six purpose-built tools — and a living document at the center that every one of them actually reads. We're looking for a few developers and QAs to put it through its paces before anyone else sees it.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p class="cue">↓ scroll for the walkthrough</p>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ PROBLEM -->
<section>
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="eyebrow">the problem</div>
    <h2>It's not a missing tool. It's tools that don't talk to each other.</h2>
    <p class="lede narrow" style="margin-top:18px; color:var(--ink-soft); font-size:16px;">
      Most of what slows a team down isn't any single broken thing — it's the seams between tools that weren't designed to know about each other.
    </p>
    <div class="pain-grid">
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="k">DOCS</div>
        <h3>Your docs don't know when your code changes.</h3>
        <p>Nothing connects the wiki to the repo — so the page and the codebase drift apart, and nobody finds out until someone trusts the wrong one.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="k">SECRETS</div>
        <h3>Your secrets don't know who's still on the team.</h3>
        <p>An API key set up in a spreadsheet three projects ago outlives the person who made it, because nothing connects your secrets to your roster.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="k">REVIEW</div>
        <h3>Your reviewer never saw the product doc.</h3>
        <p>A pull request can pass every check and still undo a decision made two months ago, because the review tool and the decision log have never talked.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pain-card">
        <div class="k">BLIND SPOTS</div>
        <h3>Nothing independent ever looks at it twice.</h3>
        <p>The tool that wrote the code and the tool that reviewed it share the same context — and nothing in the stack exists to check either one from the outside.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============================================================ IDEA -->
